WEBVTT

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:17.870
<i>hoshi ga furishikiru penthouse de
In the penthouse that watches the stars fall...</i>

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:24.040
<i>sora no ORUGO-RU hitori kiiteta
I listened to Heaven's music box...</i>

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:30.460
<i>GARASU no RO-PU wo mekakushi de wataru
Walking, blindfolded, across a tight-rope of glass...</i>

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:37.090
<i>minna sabishii SA-KASU no kodomo sa
Everyone is like, the lonely child of the circus.</i>

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:45.020
<i>hitori bocchi no kanashimi ni
The rope that creaks with the sadness of isolation...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:50.770
<i>kishinda tsuna ga kokoro de yureteru...
...is still locked deep in my heart...</i>

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>yasashii me wo shita dareka ni aitai
I wish to meet the one who's eyes glow with warmth!</i>

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:25.980
<i>sasayaite kureyo soba ni iruyotte Silent Voice
Whisper to me that you'll always be there by my side, Silent Voice.</i>

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:36.660
The La Vie en Rose
was attacked by three Jamru Fins,

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:40.230
mainly because of
Emary's feelings for Captain Bright.

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.170
Beecha was having
doubts about me,

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.310
but that was because
I hadn't explained things to him.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:48.420
In the end, the mobile armors
were just toying with the Double Zeta.

00:01:48.750 --> 00:01:50.640
Way to go, Leina!

00:01:50.640 --> 00:01:54.870
With all this, are we going to
make it to Side 3, where Haman is?

00:01:56.580 --> 00:02:00.710
THE SECOND COMING OF SARASA

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.770
We're aborting the pursuit.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:23.710
It's just a matter of time
till we catch up with them.

00:02:23.710 --> 00:02:28.060
Now that we know their
destination, there's no need to rush.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:31.280
We'll deal with them
at our leisure at Side 3.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:35.520
Showing Lady Haman the
end of this new Argama...

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.660
That will be the big event!

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:41.290
I can't be as optimistic
as Lord Mashymre.

00:02:41.290 --> 00:02:44.590
Especially about that pilot.
Judau, was it?

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:56.910
We lost them!

00:02:56.910 --> 00:02:58.110
All right!

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.480
No, they let us go.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:04.120
The enemy knows
we're headed for Core 3.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:05.270
Exactly.

00:03:05.270 --> 00:03:07.990
Meaning they can finish
us off at any time?

00:03:07.990 --> 00:03:09.970
How dare they
make fools of us!

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:12.570
In that case, we'll take out
that colony along with Haman!

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:14.050
Hold on, Beecha!

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:17.300
There are people at Side 3 who
have nothing to do with this war!

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.630
So? Who cares
about a few of them?!

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:23.000
Isn't that exactly like Haman,
who dropped a colony on Dublin?!

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.920
If we fight by involving civilians,
we're no better than they are!

00:03:26.920 --> 00:03:29.080
Hey! Now, look...!

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:31.400
Iino's right!

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:33.560
That's something you must never do!

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.430
But they're looking down on us!

00:03:35.990 --> 00:03:39.020
What happened to the guts
you had back on Shangri-La?!

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:41.690
We're now entering
visual range of Side 3.

00:03:41.690 --> 00:03:43.920
Wh-Where is it?

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.510
They should be just about
matching the angle of the sun.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:52.360
Side 3.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:55.800
Look!

00:03:57.620 --> 00:04:00.080
Iino! Magnify that
on the screen!

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:24.310
- Reminds me of when I was a trainee.
- Good job, sir!

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.710
Nahel Argama,
what are you doing?!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:35.700
That civilian vessel
is under attack!

00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:39.210
This will all be pointless if we
exhaust ourselves doing rescues...

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.280
before we even get to Core 3!

00:04:40.280 --> 00:04:42.010
What would you do, Judau?!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:45.520
You're right, Beecha, but we also
need to gather intelligence.

00:04:45.520 --> 00:04:47.260
We don't have time
to think about this!

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:50.590
Elle, stop!
The deputy captain's right.

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:52.500
They're just old Zakus out there!

00:04:52.500 --> 00:04:54.550
Oh. Really...

00:04:56.380 --> 00:04:59.350
Elle Vianno!
Gundam Mk. II, here I go!

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:04.790
Roux Louka!
Zeta, here I go!

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:15.210
You sure those
two can handle this?

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.580
Wow... you're getting pretty savvy,
aren't you, Deputy Captain?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:19.770
Of course!

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:21.130
I don't like this...

00:05:21.130 --> 00:05:23.920
Why would the Zeon Zakus
attack a civilian vessel?

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:27.730
The Neo Zeon are using everything
they have, even their old forces.

00:05:27.730 --> 00:05:29.580
That must be it.

00:05:29.780 --> 00:05:32.840
Roux and Elle aren't stupid.
We'll let them handle it.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.050
Hey, they've come out!
Are all the crates blown yet?

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.390
One to go!

00:05:44.390 --> 00:05:47.770
Okay, don't let them
suspect anything!

00:05:50.970 --> 00:05:51.820
I see them now!

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.190
Oh, I'm so scared!
They're coming this way!

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:04.930
Elle, we'll split up!
I'll get around behind them!

00:06:04.930 --> 00:06:05.790
Roger!

00:06:11.060 --> 00:06:13.750
I won't pull punches
just because you're antiques!

00:06:26.240 --> 00:06:27.870
Slippery little...!

00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:34.080
Huh?
They just flew past us!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:37.990
Of all the nerve!

00:06:37.990 --> 00:06:39.200
They're just running!

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.240
l don't like it. What's...?

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:47.330
It's about time. We'll break
past them and retreat at once!

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:49.010
Incoming!

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:50.830
They won't escape this time!

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.000
Now! Scatter!

00:06:59.320 --> 00:07:01.390
Huh? They ran?

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:03.640
What's going on?
I really don't like this!

00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:13.200
Operation completed.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.320
Hmpf! Even so, they took us
really lightly.

00:07:16.320 --> 00:07:20.150
The Newtype she's so crazy about
didn't even show up.

00:07:23.560 --> 00:07:26.610
Hmm...
this smells like a setup to me.

00:07:26.610 --> 00:07:29.620
I'm sure the enemy is just
scared of the Nahel Argama.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.140
You're with the AEUG?

00:07:46.140 --> 00:07:47.200
Yes.

00:07:47.200 --> 00:07:49.030
We appreciate the assistance.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.600
Welcome aboard the Nahel Argama.

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:52.300
Argama? It is the AEUG!

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:55.110
Okay, everyone,
please begin moving.

00:07:55.110 --> 00:07:56.710
- By the way...
- Yes?

00:07:56.710 --> 00:08:01.910
We're fleeing Side 3 in
opposition to Neo Zeon.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:05.280
But you seem to be
headed toward Side 3, so...

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:06.220
I understand.

00:08:06.220 --> 00:08:10.080
We'll get you civilians dropped
off ASAP, so you won't be involved.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:12.790
Once you're through,
please move further inside.

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:13.880
Next?

00:08:14.440 --> 00:08:16.810
Um, can you
remove the sunglasses?

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:21.650
Thanks. That'll do.

00:08:24.150 --> 00:08:26.500
We're finally done.

00:08:49.870 --> 00:08:52.300
Preparations for towing
civilian vessel, complete.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:56.170
Right! La Vie en Rose!
Are you satisfied, Miss Emary?

00:08:56.770 --> 00:09:00.370
Well done!
La Vie en Rose, launch!

00:09:05.090 --> 00:09:07.810
Nahel Argama, launch!

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:11.310
Beecha! Another civilian
vessel is under attack!

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:14.140
What?! Another one?!

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:17.810
Beecha!

00:09:18.020 --> 00:09:22.130
I know! Man, Deputy Captain
Emary's such a worrywart!

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.650
I'll go out this time.

00:09:31.750 --> 00:09:34.140
That's insanely classic
weaponry they're using.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:35.760
More than ours!

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:39.630
We found an antique as
a bonus on the way home.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:51.930
After we let them go,
the Argama's still butting in?

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.620
You're total cowards to
attack helpless opponents twice!

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.320
It's the Double Zeta!

00:09:59.320 --> 00:10:01.150
Scatter! Scatter!
Do not engage!

00:10:04.520 --> 00:10:06.920
You won't escape this time!

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.370
- It's after us!
- Never mind, just run!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.840
You can't match my acceleration!

00:10:25.740 --> 00:10:27.840
You're not taking us
without a fight!

00:10:37.350 --> 00:10:38.690
Damn you!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.150
You're not destroying that ship!

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:50.730
What?!

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:56.080
It's all because of you that she...!

00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:57.750
"She"?

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.220
What is this ship?

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:22.610
Rescuing two stranded ships
like that is a good omen!

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:24.480
That's not why you're happy, though.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.820
Wh-What do you mean?

00:11:25.820 --> 00:11:29.760
Because one of them
is from Moon Moon, right?

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.620
That's beside the point!

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:34.290
So, we were saved
by the giant yet again.

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:37.450
As it stands, we don't need
to check this ship, do we?

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:40.500
Miss Rasara, I'm really touched!

00:11:41.080 --> 00:11:42.790
I'm Sarasa.

00:11:44.950 --> 00:11:47.940
- Beecha!
- Smooth move.

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:50.090
You haven't changed, Mr. Mondo.

00:11:50.090 --> 00:11:53.380
I thought my troubles had
aged me since we last met.

00:11:53.380 --> 00:11:55.140
Please don't keep taking pictures.

00:11:55.140 --> 00:12:00.600
Everyone, my sister senses
something aboard this vessel.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:01.940
Right?

00:12:12.700 --> 00:12:13.490
Please.

00:12:13.490 --> 00:12:14.530
Thanks.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:16.120
Here.

00:12:16.120 --> 00:12:16.870
Right.

00:12:16.870 --> 00:12:18.700
Sorry, can I have two?

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:20.700
Sure. Here.

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.500
- Thanks.
- No problem.

00:12:22.500 --> 00:12:23.830
Here's another one.

00:12:23.830 --> 00:12:25.880
Thanks. Here you go.

00:12:25.880 --> 00:12:27.840
I appreciate it.

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:33.220
Please don't ask the impossible.
This is a military ship.

00:12:34.400 --> 00:12:36.010
If there's factional strife...

00:12:36.010 --> 00:12:39.140
between the colonies,
we'll have allies in Side 3, too.

00:12:39.140 --> 00:12:41.640
So you wanna go
to a neutral colony?

00:12:41.640 --> 00:12:45.730
There'll be some among
the refugees that'll help us too, right?

00:12:45.730 --> 00:12:46.480
Yes.

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:47.690
We can't do that.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:50.320
We have to always consider
that there might be spies.

00:12:50.320 --> 00:12:54.200
We checked all of the refugees!
Don't you trust us?!

00:12:54.200 --> 00:12:58.780
Except, this vessel is
filled with an evil aura.

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.950
One that tempts
people to lose their way...

00:13:01.200 --> 00:13:03.370
M-Miss Sarasa, you, too...?

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.000
- My sister's intuition is reliable.
- But...

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:08.790
Okay, we'll recheck
the refugees' IDs.

00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.590
I don't think we'll
be wasting our time.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:21.470
Well?

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:22.680
No.

00:13:22.680 --> 00:13:25.270
You don't think something's
happened to Lady Haman, do you?

00:13:25.270 --> 00:13:28.770
She came aboard this ship
personally. She must have a reason.

00:13:29.540 --> 00:13:32.690
I suppose so.
It'd be easy to just destroy it.

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:35.280
Hello, Deputy Captain here.

00:13:35.280 --> 00:13:37.200
Does anyone have
a free hand up there?!

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:39.660
We don't have enough
blankets for the refugees!

00:13:39.660 --> 00:13:41.910
Send me some help
with the laundry!

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.160
Even the machines are
giving me a hard time!

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.710
Beecha, I've got a call
for you from Elle now.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:50.130
Huh? What?
Beecha here.

00:13:50.340 --> 00:13:54.090
I... have... had... ENOUGH!

00:13:54.090 --> 00:13:58.570
You seriously expect me to
cook for 80 people all by myself?!

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:01.680
I'm ready to chop you up
and make soup out of you!

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:03.810
SEND ME SOMEONE, NOW!

00:14:03.810 --> 00:14:06.890
I'll think of something!
Get off my back!

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:07.730
Women!

00:14:07.980 --> 00:14:11.440
Can anyone please help
with the cooking and laundry?

00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:14.650
We're kind of
shorthanded on this ship.

00:14:15.340 --> 00:14:19.070
We need a few more hands.
It's for your benefit.

00:14:19.070 --> 00:14:21.240
This way.

00:14:31.730 --> 00:14:34.880
The thing is how do we
check the refugees' IDs...

00:14:34.880 --> 00:14:36.710
when we don't have
access to that data here?

00:14:36.880 --> 00:14:41.180
No problem. The La Vie en
Rose's computer will have it.

00:14:41.180 --> 00:14:43.010
Are they so well prepared?

00:14:43.010 --> 00:14:45.140
I need to hurry.

00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:17.340
Sorry for the trouble,
but we need to recheck your IDs.

00:15:22.150 --> 00:15:23.680
What's your code number, please?

00:15:23.680 --> 00:15:26.100
I'm fine, thank you.

00:15:26.100 --> 00:15:28.270
Your code number, grandpa!

00:15:28.270 --> 00:15:30.850
l don't have any kids.

00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:38.690
What's that light?!

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:40.400
It's too close to be an enemy.

00:15:40.400 --> 00:15:41.950
There wasn't an
impact, was there?

00:15:42.630 --> 00:15:45.320
Lady Haman is in danger!

00:15:54.930 --> 00:15:56.250
Mobile suits!

00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.710
What?! From where?!

00:16:03.740 --> 00:16:05.970
Attention,
pseudo-Argama!

00:16:05.970 --> 00:16:09.590
We're occupying this ship!
Do not attempt to resist!

00:16:09.590 --> 00:16:12.890
This must be what
Miss Sarasa was talking about!

00:16:12.890 --> 00:16:15.270
It's too late to realize that now!

00:16:16.750 --> 00:16:20.150
Pardon, may I see
your ID, please?

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.570
Come on, answer me.
You must have an ID.

00:16:24.570 --> 00:16:27.120
It's rude to grab a person
from behind, don't you think?

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:29.370
Then just show me your ID.

00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:40.250
- What was that?
- Is it another battle?!

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.380
I see. The enemy's been here!

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.990
Hasty child.

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:49.640
It's all according to plan, Lady Haman.

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:51.680
Mr. Mondo.

00:16:51.680 --> 00:16:52.770
Giants?!

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:54.740
Are they Neo Zeon?

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:58.860
If you'd just checked the refugees
properly, this wouldn't have happened!

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:00.820
I did!
As best as I could!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:02.990
Mr. Mondo was very diligent!

00:17:02.990 --> 00:17:04.610
Don't spoil him like that!

00:17:04.610 --> 00:17:07.030
He's the way he is because
people always do that!

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:11.410
Mr. Mondo!

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.830
What will they do
after they take over?!

00:17:16.850 --> 00:17:18.790
Mobile suit deck!

00:17:18.790 --> 00:17:20.210
Huh? Judau?

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:24.010
What?
You said that to Mondo?!

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.090
Mondo! Are you
going out there alone?

00:17:27.090 --> 00:17:29.010
- Lemme go!
- What will you do by yourself?!

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:31.430
If that's the way you want to play...

00:17:32.910 --> 00:17:36.380
Wait! If you play this wrong,
everyone'll get killed!

00:17:36.380 --> 00:17:38.600
I'll take them out
before they that happens!

00:17:38.600 --> 00:17:40.610
Are you trying to
kill yourself, Mondo?!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:44.530
It's my fault this happened.
That's why...

00:17:49.050 --> 00:17:50.950
We told you not to resist!

00:17:50.950 --> 00:17:53.410
Back up those words
with your power!

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.120
Mondo!

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:03.300
Lady Haman!

00:18:03.500 --> 00:18:05.090
Not so loud!

00:18:05.090 --> 00:18:07.220
If we stay alive,
we can wait for our chance!

00:18:07.820 --> 00:18:09.220
Did you miss on purpose?

00:18:09.400 --> 00:18:10.970
Wh-What?!

00:18:10.970 --> 00:18:12.970
I didn't mean for the
shot to be that far off!

00:18:13.220 --> 00:18:14.560
Exactly!

00:18:14.560 --> 00:18:17.730
If you like, I'll try destroying
your ship with one more shot!

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:21.560
Don't move!
I'm not bluffing! Look!

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:31.450
Whoops!
Looks like I missed.

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:35.790
I definitely saw
some kind of barrier!

00:18:37.560 --> 00:18:39.790
I swear I'll destroy
your ship for real!

00:18:39.790 --> 00:18:42.720
Do that, and you'll
be going with it!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:44.630
Is he serious?

00:18:47.730 --> 00:18:50.590
If Lady Haman wasn't on board...

00:18:51.940 --> 00:18:53.430
What's so funny?!

00:19:00.330 --> 00:19:02.190
Did you lose count of the enemy?

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:11.700
What happened
to all that spirit?!

00:19:11.700 --> 00:19:13.530
- Hold it!
- What?!

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:19.910
However many of you there are,
we're still on top of your ship!

00:19:19.910 --> 00:19:21.290
Can you fight?

00:19:21.290 --> 00:19:25.140
We're carrying civilians!
You're playing dirty!

00:19:25.140 --> 00:19:28.420
You can't deny
this is a military vessel!

00:19:29.820 --> 00:19:32.800
One move, and we
destroy your new warship!

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:37.430
These guys are trying real hard to
take the Nahel Argama unharmed.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.180
But why?

00:19:39.180 --> 00:19:42.690
Okay, now move your ship
into the center of Side 3's airspace.

00:19:42.900 --> 00:19:45.650
We'll be taking those Gundams as well.

00:19:48.710 --> 00:19:51.530
I'm going to protect this ship!

00:19:51.530 --> 00:19:54.240
Do you know what
will happen if you resist?

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:57.580
Move!

00:20:00.250 --> 00:20:02.370
What?!

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.250
Now!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.420
- Get the other guy!
- Gotcha!

00:20:13.220 --> 00:20:15.720
You had some nerve trying
to take this ship intact!

00:20:21.530 --> 00:20:24.140
I was beaten so easily?!

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:32.070
Down here!

00:20:46.520 --> 00:20:48.420
I'm not praising you.

00:20:48.420 --> 00:20:50.300
I... I know!

00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:51.800
Still, good job out there.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:54.400
You were wonderful, Mr. Mondo.

00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:57.450
My carelessness caused it,
so I had to fix it.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.970
Wow. I've changed
my opinion of you.

00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:01.390
Torres!

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:05.850
You gonna hold
her hands all day?

00:21:10.080 --> 00:21:11.900
Wait here.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:13.440
Yes.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.750
I beg your pardon.

00:21:24.140 --> 00:21:25.660
Yes?

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:27.670
You trouble me.

00:21:29.230 --> 00:21:35.800
I sense the source of all this
evil coming from your body.

00:21:35.800 --> 00:21:38.260
Source of evil, you say?

00:21:38.490 --> 00:21:43.600
But it's just a distortion
of your true self.

00:21:43.600 --> 00:21:46.980
Your feelings are
no different from Judau's.

00:21:46.980 --> 00:21:49.350
Never forget that.

00:21:49.750 --> 00:21:54.280
Nonsense. Even though
I'm here now, Judau is...!

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:59.450
I don't know who you are, my lady,
but I wish you health.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:03.040
By the teachings of light.

00:22:03.040 --> 00:22:05.160
Teachings of light?

00:22:07.350 --> 00:22:09.170
There's nothing more we can do.

00:22:09.170 --> 00:22:11.710
We should head for
Colony 24 of Side 3.

00:22:11.710 --> 00:22:13.800
They say it's a neutral colony.

00:22:13.960 --> 00:22:15.670
Yeah. We can't do anything...

00:22:15.670 --> 00:22:18.260
till we drop these
civilians off at a colony.

00:22:18.260 --> 00:22:23.430
Right! Nahel Argama,
change course and head for Colony 24!

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:28.520
We also need to gather intel
on the colony Haman's at!

00:22:44.540 --> 00:22:50.820
<i>ikuyaku ikuman ikuoku no hoshi yo
Hundreds upon thousands upon millions of stars...</i>

00:22:50.820 --> 00:22:56.950
<i>naze hikaru dake nano ka kataru chikara no shiwase
...why do you just sit there and twinkle? Show me the power that lets me connect!</i>

00:22:56.950 --> 00:23:08.050
<i>Ima nara ore demo furikaerasu ni tobitatsu kokoro
For now, even I've got a mind that wanders without reminiscing past regrets!</i>

00:23:08.940 --> 00:23:13.930
<i>Hoshi no kazu dake inochi wo takuwareba
If lives are really stored in the form of stars...</i>

00:23:14.950 --> 00:23:19.940
<i>ginga no mure no hikari wo kaete misero
...show me how to change the light and move galaxies...</i>

00:23:20.620 --> 00:23:29.650
<i>kono te ga tsukamu inochi no omosa ni naru
The weight of life itself, will be held in my hands!</i>

00:23:29.650 --> 00:23:35.530
<i>mada meinai yo sora no michishirude wa
Space's guidepost is still not within my sights...</i>

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:41.620
<i>kono te ni saware hikari isenmanen
Let the light of 10 million years touch this hand!</i>

00:23:47.100 --> 00:23:49.290
To get these rescued
civilians off the ship,

00:23:49.290 --> 00:23:51.500
we made contact
with a strange colony.

00:23:51.500 --> 00:23:56.460
Our girls dared to approach some old guy
even though they knew it was risky.

00:23:56.460 --> 00:24:01.140
In the end, Haman drops her
makeup to reveal herself!

00:24:01.140 --> 00:24:03.600
I'm not gonna
criticize peoples' tastes,

00:24:03.600 --> 00:24:05.310
but you better stay
out of our way, mister!

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:08.430
Next Time

00:24:05.310 --> 00:24:08.430
TIGERBAUM DREAM

00:24:05.930 --> 00:24:10.060
Next time, on Gundam ZZ:
"Tigerbaum Dream."

00:24:10.450 --> 00:24:12.190
Outta my way, you antiques!
